    "steps": [
        {
            "step_number": 1,
            "title": "Guitar String Replacement",
            "instruction": [
                "Rotate the tuner of the string you want to replace in a clockwise direction until it's loose.",
                "You can either do it by hand (First Picture) or you can use the guitar string winder (Second picture)."
            ],
            "image_urls": [
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/6SfHMVlctPjFclLW.medium",
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/VsTAKLXBM5ZZlJcf.medium",
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/fLlJPB1msMXR6HYk.medium"
            ],
            "thumbnails": [
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/6SfHMVlctPjFclLW.200x150",
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/VsTAKLXBM5ZZlJcf.200x150",
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/fLlJPB1msMXR6HYk.200x150"
            ],
            "edit_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/Baby+Taylor+Guitar+String+Replacement/</Guide/edit/145694/297043>",
            "add_comment_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/Baby+Taylor+Guitar+String+Replacement/<#comment>"
        },
        {
            "step_number": 2,
            "instruction": [
                "Grab a plier and pull out the bridge pin of the string you want to replace.",
                "Make sure that you've completed step 1 first. The string has to be loose before doing this step."
            ],
            "image_urls": [
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/anL44IZXA3kidjAc.medium"
            ],
            "thumbnails": [
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/anL44IZXA3kidjAc.200x150",
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/xrB3PL2lKDVKKSnA.200x150"
            ],
            "edit_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/Baby+Taylor+Guitar+String+Replacement/</Guide/edit/145694/297044>",
            "add_comment_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/Baby+Taylor+Guitar+String+Replacement/<#comment>"
        },
        {
            "step_number": 3,
            "instruction": [
                "Take out the string from the bridge and the tuning pin.",
                "You can now throw away the string. You will not be needing it anymore."
            ],
            "edit_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/Baby+Taylor+Guitar+String+Replacement/</Guide/edit/145694/297045>",
            "add_comment_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/Baby+Taylor+Guitar+String+Replacement/<#comment>"
        },
        {
            "step_number": 4,
            "instruction": [
                "Grab the new string and place the end (ball-end) inside the bridge.",
                "The ball-end of a string is the side of the string that has a ball shape. (Shown in picture 2)"
            ],
            "edit_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/Baby+Taylor+Guitar+String+Replacement/</Guide/edit/145694/297046>",
            "add_comment_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/Baby+Taylor+Guitar+String+Replacement/<#comment>"
        },
        {
            "step_number": 5,
            "instruction": [
                "Place the bridge pin inside the bridge in order to lock in the new string.",
                "Lightly hammer down the bridge pin to keep it from detaching."
            ],
            "edit_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/Baby+Taylor+Guitar+String+Replacement/</Guide/edit/145694/297047>",
            "add_comment_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/Baby+Taylor+Guitar+String+Replacement/<#comment>"
        },
        {
            "step_number": 6,
            "instruction": [
                "Cut the excess string with a plier.",
                "Cut the string around 1.5 inches over the desired tuning pin. (Recommended by Taylor Guitars)"
            ],
            "edit_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/Baby+Taylor+Guitar+String+Replacement/</Guide/edit/145694/297048>",
            "add_comment_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/Baby+Taylor+Guitar+String+Replacement/<#comment>"
        },
        {
            "step_number": 7,
            "instruction": [
                "Place the new string inside the tuning pinhole.",
                "It is recommended to place a really small portion of the string inside the pinhole to keep it from ripping your guitar bag. (As shown in the picture)"
            ],
            "edit_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/Baby+Taylor+Guitar+String+Replacement/</Guide/edit/145694/297049>",
            "add_comment_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/Baby+Taylor+Guitar+String+Replacement/<#comment>"
        },
        {
            "step_number": 8,
            "instruction": [
                "Rotate the tuners in a counter-clockwise direction to tighten the new string.",
                "You can either tighten it by hand (First Picture) or you can use the guitar string winder (Second Picture)."
            ],
            "edit_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/Baby+Taylor+Guitar+String+Replacement/</Guide/edit/145694/297050>",
            "add_comment_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/Baby+Taylor+Guitar+String+Replacement/<#comment>"
        },
        {
            "step_number": 9,
            "instruction": [
                "Make sure your string is in tune and strum away!"
            ],
            "edit_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/Baby+Taylor+Guitar+String+Replacement/</Guide/edit/145694/297051>",
            "add_comment_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/Baby+Taylor+Guitar+String+Replacement/<#comment>"
        }
    ],
    "conclusion": {
        "text": "Most guitar strings de-tune after they’ve been recently replaced. Tune your strings every once in a while for a few days and the strings will stay in tune.",
        "author_points": "Give the author +30 points!  You're Finished!",
